{"id": "inv1-neg-base-unproved", "rules": ["INV-1"], "expect": {"kind": "reject", "rule": "INV-1"}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "A zero-trip counted range still reaches its first loop header, so INV-1 must prove the invariant base case without assuming the same invariant. The false relation 1 <= 0 is rejected before lowering."}
{"id": "inv1-neg-backedge-unproved", "rules": ["INV-1", "SET-1"], "expect": {"kind": "reject", "rule": "INV-1"}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "The base case holds, but an arbitrary normal body fallthrough writes sum = 2 before the next header. INV-1 rejects the unproved backedge rather than checking one selected iteration or retaining a runtime test."}
{"id": "inv1-neg-repeated-name", "rules": ["INV-1"], "expect": {"kind": "reject", "rule": "INV-1"}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "Two invariants in one counted-loop header use the same proof-only name. INV-1 rejects the second declaration deterministically in the separate invariant domain; invariant names create neither runtime bindings nor an overloaded lookup."}
{"id": "inv1-pos-ordinary-loop-guarded-cursor", "rules": ["INV-1", "ENT-3", "ENT-5", "ENT-6", "SET-1"], "expect": {"kind": "run", "exit": 0}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "An ordinary loop header bounds a cursor the body increments under a source guard. The writer publishes the guard as a body invariant on the reaching path while its premises are still live; that affine conclusion over the pre-write value images survives the SET-1 target kill and discharges the backedge on its own, alongside the automatic commit-value route the neighbouring plain-set case isolates."}
{"id": "inv1-pos-ordinary-loop-cursor-set-image", "rules": ["INV-1", "ENT-3", "ENT-5", "SET-1"], "expect": {"kind": "run", "exit": 0}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "The same ordinary loop header bounds a cursor the body increments with a plain set. The commit evaluates its right-hand side to that occurrence's commit value before the SET-1 target kill, so the pre-kill closure carries the guarded bound onto that value and the post-write equality names it at the backedge; no republished body invariant is needed, and the two spellings of one value agree."}
{"id": "prf1-pos-explicit-affine-proof", "rules": ["PRF-1", "FN-8", "FN-9", "OP-2", "ENT-3", "SET-1"], "expect": {"kind": "run", "exit": 0}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "Three independent component bounds exceed AUTO's two-premise boundary, so a source-written certificate names all three in order. Its sum directly implies the slightly weaker local invariant; that published fact and the aggregate limit prove both exact additions and the callee postcondition, an unrelated assignment does not change its value images, and the caller uses the verified postcondition for one more exact addition."}
{"id": "prf1-pos-explicit-factor", "rules": ["PRF-1", "ENT-3"], "expect": {"kind": "run", "exit": 0}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "AUTO first publishes a two-component bound. A later certificate names that invariant once with the explicit factor three, and PRF-1 checks the scaled sum without repeated uses or multiplier search."}
{"id": "prf1-pos-integer-tightening-midpoint", "rules": ["PRF-1", "INV-1", "ENT-6", "OP-4"], "expect": {"kind": "run", "exit": 0}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "A binary-search midpoint. The unsigned literal division publishes the scaled quotient image, and the written certificate sums it with the ordered endpoints into 2*(mid - hi) <= -1. Halving that accumulated sum and taking the mathematical floor of its bound is the one integer consequence PRF-1 admits, and the halved midpoint relation with the verified room requirement discharges the subscript."}
{"id": "prf1-neg-unproved-premise", "rules": ["PRF-1", "FN-8", "ENT-3"], "expect": {"kind": "reject", "rule": "PRF-1"}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "The first written use relation is absent from the pre-proof context. PRF-1 rejects that premise in source order; the written conclusion creates neither a fact nor a runtime fallback."}
{"id": "prf1-neg-inexact-combination", "rules": ["PRF-1", "FN-8"], "expect": {"kind": "reject", "rule": "PRF-1"}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "Both written premises are available, but their coefficient-one sum proves x <= 254 while the target requires x <= 253. The final DIRECT check permits weakening, not strengthening, and PRF-1 never retries with another combination."}
{"id": "prf1-neg-fact-killed-by-write", "rules": ["PRF-1", "ENT-5", "OP-2"], "expect": {"kind": "reject", "rule": "OP-2"}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "A three-premise certificate proves a relation over the pre-assignment value images. Assigning a new first component does not make that theorem false, but the theorem says nothing about the replacement image, so the later exact addition remains unproved and OP-2 rejects."}
{"id": "prf1-neg-duplicate-use", "rules": ["PRF-1"], "expect": {"kind": "reject", "rule": "PRF-1"}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "A non-AUTO scaled target repeats the same normalized named premise. PRF-1 rejects the second occurrence regardless of factor; one explicit multiplier is the only canonical scaling form."}
{"id": "prf1-neg-explicit-factor-one", "rules": ["PRF-1"], "expect": {"kind": "reject", "rule": "PRF-1"}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "A non-AUTO scaled target writes an explicit proof factor of one. PRF-1 rejects that noncanonical spelling because omission alone denotes coefficient one."}
{"id": "prf1-neg-redundant-use-block", "rules": ["PRF-1", "ENT-3"], "expect": {"kind": "reject", "rule": "PRF-1"}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "The local invariant target is already established by AUTO from one requirement. PRF-1 rejects the entire nonempty use block as redundant; removing the block is the deterministic repair."}
{"id": "op4-neg-external-index-without-fact", "rules": ["OP-4", "ENT-6", "SYS-2"], "expect": {"kind": "reject", "rule": "OP-4"}, "status": "runnable", "doc": "A system result is an ordinary symbolic runtime value, not a fact source. Using it directly as a buffer index leaves the bounds Goal unproved, so OP-4 rejects before lowering."}
