{"rule": "OWN-8", "covered_by": "policy", "reason": "Reject-when-unsure is the checker's global disposition, not a program-checkable constraint: it is never emitted as a standalone 'OWN-8' verdict. Every OWN reject case in this cluster (own1/3/4/5/10/11/12-neg) IS an instance of it \u2014 each names the specific rule and, per the spec, the restructuring. A sound-but-unprovable program is still rejected, but the diagnostic cites the concrete rule, so there is no source->verdict pair that asserts OWN-8 itself."}
{"rule": "OWN-9", "covered_by": "policy", "reason": "OWN-9 is explicitly a non-normative optimizer consequence, not a source-to-verdict rule. It states facts licensed by OWN-5 exclusivity; the positive and negative ownership cases exercise the source guarantees from which an optimizer may later derive those facts, without asserting that the current backend emits a particular attribute."}
